Steps to memorize for exam
1. Create Maven Web Project
   
   File → New → Maven Project
2. Select Webapp Archetype
   
   Search webapp → Select maven-archetype-webapp → Version 1.4 → Click Next.
3. Enter Project Details
   
   - Group Id: SE
   - Artifact Id: MavenWeb
   
   Click Finish.
4. Open JSP File
   
   MavenWeb → src → main → webapp → index.jsp
   
   This is the main JSP page.
5. Add Servlet Dependency
   
   Open pom.xml → Search Servlet API in MVN Repository → Copy dependency → Paste inside <dependencies> → Save.
6. Add Tomcat Server
   
   Window → Show View → Servers → Click create new server → Select Apache Tomcat v9.0 → Choose Tomcat installation folder → Finish.
7. Configure Tomcat
   
   Double-click Tomcat in Servers tab → Select Use Tomcat Installation → Set HTTP port to 8085 → Save.
8. Build Maven Project
   
   Right-click project → Run As → Maven Build
   
   Goals:
   
   bash     clean install test     
   
   Click Apply → Run.
   
   Check BUILD SUCCESS.
9. Deploy on Tomcat
   
   Right-click index.jsp → Run As → Run on Server → Select Tomcat → Click Finish.
10. Check Browser Output
    
    Open:
    
    text     http://localhost:8085/MavenWeb/     
    
    The Hello World page should appear.
Quick memory flow
New Maven → Webapp 1.4 → Project IDs → index.jsp → Servlet Dependency → Tomcat Setup → Maven Build → Run on Server → Browser

Remember:
- Group Id: SE
- Artifact Id: MavenWeb
- Tomcat HTTP port: 8085
- Browser URL: localhost:8085/MavenWeb/
Note: For Tomcat 9, use javax.servlet-api. Tomcat 10 and later use jakarta.servlet-api.
